==French==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|frm|fr}} {{m|frm|suyvre}}, from {{etyl|fro|fr}} {{m|fro|sivre}}, {{m|fro|siure}}, from {{etyl|VL.|fr}} {{m|la|*sequio}}, from {{etyl|la|fr}} {{m|la|sequī}}, present active infinitive of {{m|la|sequor}}, cognate with Portuguese/Spanish: ''[[seguir]]''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{fr-IPA}}
* {{audio|Fr-suivre.ogg|audio|lang=fr}}
* {{a|Louisiana}} {{IPA|/sɥiv(r)/|/sɥir/|/swir/|lang=fr}}

===Verb===
{{fr-verb}}

# to [[follow]] (literal sense)
#: ''Je t'invite à me '''suivre.'''''
#:: I invite you '''to follow''' me.
# to [[follow]]; to [[get]] (figurative sense; to understand what someone is saying)
#: ''Il nous faut travailler dur. Tu me '''suis''' ?''
#:: We have to work hard. '''Do''' you '''get''' me?
# to [[take]] (a course or a class)
#: ''Ma sœur '''suit''' un cours d'italien.''
#:: My sister '''is taking''' an Italian course.

